  "description": "Tests 10 and 11, derived by hand from 6.8 and 7 with a scripted r = RandomDoubleRangeUniform(0, 100) (the 'rng' event; its arguments are checked). Shipped tuning: random fire probability 5, curve f(40) = 7. r = 3 < 5 and a random lot whose building is at world (100, 200): PositionToCell -> (6, 12), IgniteCell(6, 12, true, false, 0) then SetCause(5). r = 3 with no lot, and with a lot without a building: the hotspot test runs with the same r; the hotspot (7, 9, 40) has f(40) = 7 > 3 -> IgniteCell(7 * 1 + 0, 9 * 1 + 0, false, false, 0) (one hotspot: no rand() call). r = 6 -> hotspot fire, no lot query (6 >= 5); r = 7 -> no fire (7 > 7 is false). Tutorial: no draw and no fire. No curve: only random fires (r = 0 queries a lot, none) and no shuffle. [choice] without a fire manager neither IgniteCell nor SetCause happens. Test 11: an EndOfCycle that reaches the hotspot test with 4 hotspots makes 3 shuffle calls; the wrap then makes 1. On a 32 x 32 map (count 1024, step 977, tractsPerDay 25) the order is shuffle then reset: rand() = 41, 18467, 6334 (shuffle), 26500 -> start 26500 mod 1024 = 900; after 25 visits current = (900 + 25 * 977) mod 1024 = 749 (the reverse order would give 914). With r < prob and a building found there is no shuffle: only the wrap's call. Shuffle order from CRT state 10: rand() = 71, 16899, 3272 -> [3, 1, 0, 2] (foundations 12.3), so with every hotspot qualifying (a one-point curve 60 > r = 50) the fourth hotspot burns first. The real generator (seeded 0; its double path takes the process clock, here 1) draws RandomDoubleRangeUniform(0, 100) at 24-bit precision (foundations 6.1, G1): mul = 0x278DDE6D, u = r24(r24(i * 2^-32) + 0.5), r = r24(u * 100) = 65.45084381103516 (the full-double value 65.45084968674928 is wrong under foundations 18).",
